---
import example from '../../lib/explainers/relational-intro.json';
---
<figure class="relational-query paper-surface" id="order-query" aria-labelledby="order-query-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Worked example · SQL and result</span>
  <h3 id="order-query-title">What is in order O12?</h3>
  <p class="example-intro">Match each order line to its product by <code>product_id</code>. Keep the quantity and price paid from the order line. All prices are euros per item.</p>
  <div class="input-tables">
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Products source table">
      <table>
        <caption>Products · current catalogue</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">product_id</th><th scope="col">name</th><th scope="col">current_price</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{example.products.map(p => <tr><td>{p.product_id}</td><td>{p.name}</td><td>€{p.current_price}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Order lines source table">
      <table>
        <caption>Order lines · recorded at purchase</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">order_id</th><th scope="col">product_id</th><th scope="col">quantity</th><th scope="col">price_paid</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{example.order_lines.map(l => <tr><td>{l.order_id}</td><td>{l.product_id}</td><td>{l.quantity}</td><td>€{l.price_paid}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="query-operation">
    <p class="example-label">The query · match IDs, select order O12</p>
    <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="SQL query for order O12"><code>{example.query}</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="table-scroll query-result" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Query result">
    <table>
      <caption>Result · two order lines</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">name</th><th scope="col">quantity</th><th scope="col">price_paid</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{example.result.map(r => <tr><td>{r.name}</td><td>{r.quantity}</td><td>€{r.price_paid}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <figcaption>The query returns two mugs at €18 each and one bowl at €24. It reads the product names from the catalogue, but the purchase prices from the order lines. The mug’s current €20 price does not enter the result. This example is displayed, not editable.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .relational-query { margin:2rem 0; padding:1.25rem; font:.85rem/1.65 var(--font-sans); }
  h3 { font:500 1.5rem/1.3 var(--font-serif); margin:0 0 .8rem; }
  .example-intro { font-size:.85rem; margin:0 0 1.4rem; }
  .input-tables { display:grid; gap:1.25rem; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x:auto; }
  table { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); }
  caption { text-align:left; font-weight:600; padding:0 0 .6rem; }
  th,td { text-align:left; padding:.55rem .5rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); white-space:nowrap; }
  th { font:500 .72rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
  .query-operation { margin:1.5rem 0; }
  .example-label { margin-bottom:.5rem; font-size:.8rem; }
  pre { overflow-x:auto; padding:1rem; font:.78rem/1.65 var(--font-mono); background:var(--color-surface); border-left:2px solid var(--color-rule-strong); margin:0; }
  pre code { background:none; padding:0; font:inherit; }
  .query-result { border-left:3px solid var(--teal); padding-left:.75rem; }
  figcaption { margin:1rem 0 0; padding-top:1rem; border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); font-size:.8rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  :focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--teal); outline-offset:4px; }
  @media(max-width:550px) { .relational-query{padding:.85rem} th,td{padding:.5rem .3rem} }
</style>
